'''Despair''' are a set of throwing knives with micronic edges, used by the [[Stalker]].

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*Capable of using the thrown-exclusive mod {{M|Concealed Explosives}}.

{{Advantages|
*[[Silent]].
}}

{{Disadvantages|
*Projectiles have travel time and travel in an arc, making it hard to hit at longer ranges and achieve headshots.
}}
{{Acquisition|Despair's blueprint is dropped by both [[Stalker]] and [[Shadow Stalker]]. It is also included in the [[What Stalker?]] bundle for {{pc|725}} in the market.}}
{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

This weapon can be sold for {{cc|5,000}}.

==Incarnon Genesis==
{{Transclude|Despair Incarnon Genesis#Acquisition}}

{{Transclude|Despair Incarnon Genesis#Incarnon Genesis}}

==Tips==
*Using the {{M|Pistol Ammo Mutation}} mod can help with ammo economy.
**Alternatively, bring along [[Squad Ammo Restore]].
*For effective use of non-hitscan weapons, it is strongly recommended to learn how to aim ahead of your target so the projectile takes into account travel time.

==Trivia==
*A "monofilament" is a type of wire or edge, consisting of a single strand or side of strongly bound together molecules. This creates an edge that is micron or even nanometer thin, the sharpest possible.
**Typically, they are applied as a cutting tool or a weapon that can sever nearly any object or other molecules.
**Organic molecular wires have been proposed for usage in optoelectronics.
*Similarly to the {{Weapon|Hikou}} and {{Weapon|Kunai}}, the Despair is a secondary thrown weapon that deals mostly {{D|Puncture}} damage.

